{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U15", "U35", "U22"],
      "pins": ["U15.2", "U35.2", "U22.4"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_SINK_ALL (chain node between U22.4/U15.2 and U15.4/U35.2)", "U22.4-U15.2 via R51", "U15.4-U35.2 via R62"],
      "obs": "On the 'LED Enable and E-Stop Config' sheet the three SN74LVC1G07 sink buffers are wired as a series chain: U22's input pin is tied to GND, but U15's input pin is tied (through R51 10K) to U22's open-drain output, and U35's input pin is tied (through R62 10K) to U15's output. Only the first buffer in the chain has its input grounded.",
      "expected": "The specification states these parts are 'wired as /OE-controlled sinks' for the independent sink points ESTOP_SINK1/ESTOP_SINK2/ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL, i.e. each buffer's input should be tied to GND so that asserting its /OE alone makes it sink and light its own branch indicator.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "an e-stop loop with multiple sink points (ESTOP_SINK1, ESTOP_SINK2, ESTOP_SINK_LOCAL) gated through single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as /OE-controlled sinks, feeding an ESTOP_OUT signal"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Sheet 'LED Enable and E-Stop Config': U22 pin2=GND; U15 pin2 -> R51 10K -> U22 pin4; U35 pin2 -> R62 10K -> U15 pin4; U35 pin4 -> R63 -> ESTOP_SINK_ALL"}
      ],
      "impact": "Because U15 and U35 do not have their inputs grounded, their outputs only sink when the preceding buffer in the chain is also sinking. A single e-stop branch being pressed/disconnected therefore fails to pull ESTOP_SINK_ALL low, fails to enable U36/ESTOP_OUT, and fails to light that branch's own LED_RED indicator. The e-stop loop no longer behaves as the independent per-branch sinks the design intends (and the changelog's 'indicator lights for each branch' goal is not met).",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the specification's e-stop description: the SN74LVC1G07 buffers U15 and U35 are chained to the previous buffer's output instead of having their inputs tied to GND as independent /OE-controlled sinks, so a single e-stop branch cannot assert ESTOP_OUT or light its own indicator. Other flagged items (16 MHz crystals, LTC4412 ideal diode, GLOBAL_EN switch, USB-diode and PoE notes) match the documented reference and are not reported."
}

